7. Discussion and Future Work

We have delivered a fully rigorous foundation for OMH. Future work includes:

· Experimental validation on the GDF platform, measuring MCM across training (Paper B).
· Philosophical implications of gauge equivalence for machine intelligence (Paper C).
· Extensions: partial observability; learnability guarantees; exact characterization of the gauge group for complex tasks.

The relationship with existing safe RL and CBF literature has been clarified: OMH subsumes the CBF penalty as a special case but provides a unified metric for optimality and compliance. The quantitative Theorem 1 gives a direct link between performance loss and MCM, making OMH testable in finite experiments.

